# Interpreter-throw closure item 6 (steps/interpreter-throw-20261010.md): a method executes its own named Structure
# whose procedure throws the implicit `convert` (the initializer edge int -> size_t refuses -1, as in
# unit_b3_init_conv_range); the procedure is on the status channel and the method, closed over it, routes the status
# as a call's: its own `catch: convert ()` takes it (before: "lmx: invariant: executing a named Structure reported a
# status", abort).  Exit 5; 7 would mean the execution completed.
fn: m () int
    S:
        int: x -1
        size_t: s (x)
    int: got 0
    ---
        S()
        got: 7
    ---
    catch: convert ()
        got: 5
return: got
int: r m()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
